e trade initiative, a centerpiece of US economic engagement with sub-Saharan Africa.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Uganda begins withdrawing troops from Somalia after two decades</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:168de86d4ba5b0df0ddfd7ee3774abe923a785237b92d6b6c960b3192bf96a2a</id><updated>2026-11-04T06:43:01Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T12:19:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/uganda-begins-withdrawing-troops-from-somalia-after-two-decades/a-79829903--679d18eec17e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/uganda-begins-withdrawing-troops-from-somalia-after-two-decades/a-79829903?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ugandan troops first deployed to Somalia in 2007 as part of an international military coalition to battle Islamic insurgents. But the mission has faced mounting pressure since a US decision to withdraw funding.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Will renewed conflict derail Ethiopia's economic growth?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a102b677a2e73eff4237197713f83d563ac813a66d55aafcdb1dbe82aa63160a</id><updated>2026-11-04T06:43:01Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T11:19:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/will-renewed-conflict-derail-ethiopia-s-economic-growth/a-79807060--aec9783cc542.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/will-renewed-conflict-derail-ethiopia-s-economic-growth/a-79807060?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ethiopia's economy is growing strongly. But renewed fighting in the north of the BRICS member state could deter investment, strain public finances and push up the cost of living.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
